  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "Read Hippy engine DOM/CSS through the existing local debug server. List targets first and retain targetId. Prefer query_nodes for exact AND filters and capture_snapshot for combined DOM/style/layout reads. Capture before and after an operation, then diff_snapshots locally to return only changes. Snapshots are bounded in-memory records, not atomic engine snapshots; consistent means no invalidation was observed, not proof that every change is reported. Reconnection creates a new session and cross-session diffs are rejected. Layout findings are evidence-based clues, not proof of pixel visibility. Read the DOM before choosing nodeIds; IDs may become stale or be reused after navigation/reload. All tools issue only four fixed read commands: no JavaScript evaluation, style edits, app reload or input. Never use document.activeElement: this is a Hippy engine node tree, not browser DOM. Native TV focus and Vue business state may not be exposed. The upstream debug server resets debugger/runtime domains on WebSocket open/close; connections are reused. No ADB fallback.",
  "durationMs": 5851,
  "stderr": ""
}
